From 5d6888b5e4023dbce2448dbe1fc4e1182bce2bb5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nicholas Smith <nsmith@tenstorrent.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 17:18:07 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [feat] Opt-in model-owned recurrent state for prefix caching

agentic-models patch P4 (vllm-tt-plugin-prefix-cache-model-recurrent-state.patch).

A hybrid model declaring
model_capabilities['prefix_cache_recurrent_state_in_model']=True snapshots its
own recurrent state, so with --enable-prefix-caching it uses plain attention
APC: mamba_cache_mode != 'none' is renormalized with
_renormalize_mamba_cache_config (m4 0001 semantics) and _install_prefix_hit_clip()
(m6) wraps KVCacheManager.get_computed_blocks. The clip returns vLLM's result
unless the adapter registers vllm_tt_plugin.prefix_hit_clip. Base: m6's
uncommitted platform.py patch with the trigger merged from m4 0001. m4's own
trigger (supports_prefix_caching, which K2 declares) is not used.

Undeclared, or with prefix caching off, the config and KVCacheManager are left
as at f6fe76b.

Tests: tests/test_prefix_cache_model_state.py; tests/conftest.py restores
KVCacheManager.get_computed_blocks after each test so the clip cannot leak.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
